# Later rules override earlier ones, so the catch-all goes first and the
# firmware exceptions after it.

# Source and text: normalise to LF in the repository. GitHub Pages serves these
# directly, and mixed endings make diffs unreadable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Firmware must never be line-ending converted.
#
# Git guesses text vs binary by sniffing content. It guessed right this time -
# it offered to convert latest.json and the .hex but left the .update.bin alone
# - but a guess is not worth relying on when the consequence is a corrupted
# image: a .update.bin with CRLF substituted for LF fails its CRC, and a
# mangled .hex gets written to a tracker over SWD.
#
# Marking them explicitly removes the guess.
*.bin binary
*.uf2 binary
*.hex -text
